      "content": "The quiet space isn't an ending; it's a cessation of the exhausting performance you've been putting on for years. Struggling against the nothingness is like trying to hold water in a sieve—it's futile and painful. If the fight itself is the source of the suffering, then the most compassionate thing you can do is stop fighting. Just allow the exhaustion to settle, and see what happens when you finally stop pushing back against the void.",
